# docs/multicolumn-plan.md D1/D4/D5. POSITIONS, NOT COUNTS: the defect
# is a lowering that shows the WRONG panes. THE EXTREMES ONLY, since the
# three-pane floors disagree (Material 1200dp, GNOME 860sp, WinUI above
# 641): 1400 is above every floor, 360 below every boundary, and
# check-steps holds the band. The MIDDLE rung is each lane's own gate
# (tools/check-pane-ladder.py is the macOS one).
expect_entries 0
expect_title "panes"
expect_panes
# The two empty slots are visible COLUMNS but not PANES (D1: a pane is a
# surface from this window's stack), which is why this reads "regular/0".
resize_window 1400x800
expect_panes "regular/0"
click button#0
expect_entries 1
expect_panes "regular/0,1"
click button#1
expect_entries 2
expect_panes "regular/0,1,2"
# All three AT ONCE, from each platform's REAL tree: the model reads
# above pass for an arm that ran and drew nothing.
expect_ax label#0 "label/root pane"
expect_ax label#1 "label/content pane"
expect_ax label#last "label/detail pane"
# Fully spread, the top covers nothing, so the verb refuses to drive an
# affordance the screen does not offer (DESIGN.md's back rule).
back
expect_entries 2
expect_panes "regular/0,1,2"
resize_window 360x600
expect_panes "compact/2"
back
expect_entries 1
expect_panes "compact/1"
back
expect_entries 0
expect_panes "compact/0"
resize_window 1400x800
expect_panes "regular/0"
